# This file exists on purpose. Without an .npmignore, npm falls back to
# .gitignore, which ignores web/out/ (the built Next.js OAuth connect frontend).
# That stripped web/out/ out of the published tarball even though package.json's
# "files" array lists it — so the hosted HTTP server shipped without the connect
# page and /oauth/connect returned 503.
#
# What actually gets published is controlled by the "files" whitelist in
# package.json (dist/, web/out/, README.md, skills/, LICENSE). This .npmignore is
# intentionally minimal so it does not re-exclude web/out/.
